# Per-model generation limits for the vision suite, think-on.
#
# These are NOT interchangeable. A single value across models is wrong in both
# directions: it wastes context on models that terminate early and truncates the
# ones that do not. Derived from the maximum observed VALID prompt+eval per model,
# rounded up with headroom — re-derive when a payload or prompt changes, and use
# the harness's own diagnostic (it prints the required num_ctx) rather than
# guessing.
#
#   model        max valid prompt+eval   ->  num_predict / num_ctx
#   gemma4:31b            10,691             12000 / 16384
#   nemotron3:33b         16,421             16000 / 24576
#   qwen3.6:35b-a3b       does not terminate    see note
#
# qwen3.6 note: on scene_single and multi_3img it has never terminated at any
# window tried (13,771 @16k, 16,000 @24.5k, done_reason=length each time). Its
# thinking is CORRECT — it names all six labels and the serial in the first 600
# characters — then spends tens of thousands of tokens re-checking bounding boxes
# without ever closing. Raising the window further is not obviously the fix; the
# open question is whether it terminates at all on these two probes. Until that is
# answered, treat those two cells as unmeasured rather than tuning a number.
#
# Think-off needs none of this: every model terminates in a few hundred tokens.

VS_NUM_PREDICT_OFF=4000
VS_NUM_CTX_OFF=16384

VS_THINKON_gemma4=12000:16384
VS_THINKON_nemotron3=16000:24576
VS_THINKON_qwen3_6=32000:40960
VS_THINKON_DEFAULT=16000:24576
